the Han dynasty (202 BCE - 220 CE) into Central Asia around 114 BCE."}, {"id": "B", "text": "In fact, some scholars criticise or even dismiss the idea of silk roads and call for a new definition or alternate term."}, {"id": "C", "text": "The Silk Road derives its name from the highly lucrative trade of silk textiles that were primarily produced in China."}, {"id": "D", "text": "The Silk Road was a network of Asian trade routes active from the second century BCE until the mid-15th century."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Silk Road", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silk_Road', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M20-CE007', 'B', ARRAY['B']::TEXT[], 'The correct quotation states that some scholars criticize or dismiss the term.', '{"D": "This sentence defines the network and its dates.", "C": "This sentence explains the name''s origin.", "A": "This sentence describes the network''s beginning."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, external_id, assessments, section, domain, skill, difficulty, format, stimulus, prompt, choices, figure_metadata, source_id, source_name, license, attribution, is_released_practice_set, status) VALUES ('RW-M20-CI008', 'HDSAT-RW-M20-CI008', ARRAY['SAT', 'PSAT/NMSQT', 'PSAT 10', 'PSAT 8/9']::TEXT[], 'Reading and Writing', 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'Medium', 'multiple_choice', 'The Library of Alexandria in Alexandria, Egypt, was one of the largest and most significant libraries of the ancient world. The library was part of a larger research institution called the Mouseion, which was dedicated to the Muses, the nine goddesses of the arts. The idea of the library in Alexandria may have been proposed by Demetrius of Phalerum, an exiled Athenian statesman living in Alexandria, to Ptolemy I Soter, who may have established plans for the library, but the library itself was probably not built until the reign of his son Ptolemy II Philadelphus. The library quickly acquired many papyrus scrolls, owing largely to the Ptolemaic kings'' aggressive and well-funded policies for procuring texts. It is unknown how many scrolls were housed at any given time at the Library of Alexandria, but estimates range from 40,000 to 700,000. Alexandria came to be regarded as the capital of knowledge and learning in part because of the Great Library.', 'Which choice best states the main idea of the text?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "The library''s holdings have been precisely counted at 700,000 scrolls."}, {"id": "B", "text": "The library was built before the Mouseion and independent of it."}, {"id": "C", "text": "The Library of Alexandria was a major ancient research library whose collection size remains uncertain."}, {"id": "D", "text": "The Library of Alexandria was a small private collection owned by Ptolemy I."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Library of Alexandria", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Library_of_Alexandria', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M20-CI008', 'C', ARRAY['C']::TEXT[], 'The passage describes the library''s importance, its origins, and the uncertainty about its holdings.', '{"D": "The text calls it one of the largest and most significant libraries of the ancient world.", "A": "The text says estimates range from 40,000 to 700,000.", "B": "The text says the library was part of the larger Mouseion."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, external_id, assessments, section, domain, skill, difficulty, format, stimulus, prompt, choices, figure_metadata, source_id, source_name, license, attribution, is_released_practice_set, status) VALUES ('RW-M20-INF008', 'HDSAT-RW-M20-INF008', ARRAY['SAT', 'PSAT/NMSQT', 'PSAT 10', 'PSAT 8/9']::TEXT[], 'Reading and Writing', 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'Medium', 'multiple_choice', 'The Library of Alexandria in Alexandria, Egypt, was one of the largest and most significant libraries of the ancient world. The library was part of a larger research institution called the Mouseion, which was dedicated to the Muses, the nine goddesses of the arts. The idea of the library in Alexandria may have been proposed by Demetrius of Phalerum, an exiled Athenian statesman living in Alexandria, to Ptolemy I Soter, who may have established plans for the library, but the library itself was probably not built until the reign of his son Ptolemy II Philadelphus. The library quickly acquired many papyrus scrolls, owing largely to the Ptolemaic kings'' aggressive and well-funded policies for procuring texts. It is unknown how many scrolls were housed at any given time at the Library of Alexandria, but estimates range from 40,000 to 700,000. Alexandria came to be regarded as the capital of knowledge and learning in part because of the Great Library.
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M20-INF008', 'D', ARRAY['D']::TEXT[], 'The wide range of estimates shows that the exact size of the collection is unknown.', '{"C": "A wide range of estimates implies uncertainty about the actual number.", "B": "The text presents 700,000 as one estimate, not a confirmed figure.", "A": "The text says the low estimate is 40,000."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
